WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.417 --> 00:00:06.625
There is the Parliament,

00:00:06.792 --> 00:00:11.625
there is the European Council
with the Council of Ministers,

00:00:11.792 --> 00:00:13.500
there is the European Commission.

00:00:13.709 --> 00:00:17.750
All the institutions have to
cooperate and collaborate.

00:00:20.041 --> 00:00:23.583
My name is Martin Schulz. I am the
President of the European Parliament.

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:28.999
My name is José Manuel Durao Barroso.

00:00:29.125 --> 00:00:31.166
I'm President of
the European Commission.

00:00:32.083 --> 00:00:38.250
I am Eleni Mavrou. I chair
the Justice and Home Affairs Council.

00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:42.250
I chaired the Economic Council.
It is called ECOFIN.

00:00:44.291 --> 00:00:45.583
I'm Herman Van Rompuy,

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.625
the President of the European Council
of the Heads of State or Government.

00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:09.333
The European Council is
a European institution

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:14.083
comprising the Heads of State or
Government of the 27 Member States,

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.709
soon to be 28 Member States.

00:01:16.875 --> 00:01:18.792
We meet four times a year.

00:01:18.959 --> 00:01:22.083
More often during a crisis period,
six or seven times a year.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.667
Together we must bring Europe back on
the path to structural growth and jobs.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:29.667
In fact, we give the overall directions

00:01:30.041 --> 00:01:33.166
of economic policy and foreign policy.

00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:35.999
We are the ultimate
political institution.

00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:48.250
The European Commission represents
the general European interest.

00:01:48.417 --> 00:01:50.375
That is the way we see ourselves.

00:01:51.458 --> 00:01:54.667
It is a unique institution
with its supranational nature.

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:56.959
We come from all our member states

00:01:57.083 --> 00:02:00.125
but we are not representing
our governments or countries.

00:02:00.291 --> 00:02:03.375
We are here to try to interpret,

00:02:03.542 --> 00:02:07.542
to represent the general
common European interest.

00:02:09.333 --> 00:02:11.750
It is the European Commission
that has the right,

00:02:11.917 --> 00:02:15.375
and I could say also the duty,
to present proposals for legislation.

00:02:15.542 --> 00:02:18.667
Afterwards the Council,
where the governments are represented,

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:22.625
and the Parliament, approve them.
They are the co–legislators.

00:02:22.792 --> 00:02:25.875
But the right of initiative
is the Commission's.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:44.166
The Council of Ministers
meets in various formations.

00:02:44.333 --> 00:02:47.959
It is the house
of the 27 Member States.

00:02:48.083 --> 00:02:51.333
It is where ministers
from each country meet.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:58.917
In each case, the ministers responsible
for specific fields take part.

00:02:59.375 --> 00:03:00.834
And when a compromise is made,

00:03:00.999 --> 00:03:03.834
on the basis of a proposal
from the Commission,

00:03:03.999 --> 00:03:06.333
we will negotiate with
the European Parliament.

00:03:15.583 --> 00:03:19.375
The Parliament represents
the citizens of the EU.

00:03:19.542 --> 00:03:23.999
Here the people need to be
in constant dialogue with each other.

00:03:25.083 --> 00:03:28.834
We are, above all, the only
legislative chamber in the world

00:03:28.999 --> 00:03:33.500
that makes binding laws
for 27 countries and nations.

00:03:33.792 --> 00:03:35.166
Who is in favour?

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.583
Who is against?

00:03:39.041 --> 00:03:41.583
Who abstains?
It is approved.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:47.500
We are a parliament with more than
700 members in 7 political groups,

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:50.166
which, I think, represent
a total of 300 parties

00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:54.041
and accommodating them all
is a huge challenge,

00:03:54.208 --> 00:04:00.041
but it's also a symbol of
what is fascinating about Europe,

00:04:00.208 --> 00:04:04.667
namely being different
and, at the same time, being united.

00:04:10.458 --> 00:04:14.959
I would say my role
is that of President

00:04:15.083 --> 00:04:18.000
but also that of a facilitator.

00:04:18.166 --> 00:04:23.917
Someone who has to act in such a way
that agreement is ultimately reached,

00:04:24.041 --> 00:04:29.500
because each European Council has to
reach an agreement, reach a compromise.

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:31.375
You have to be well prepared

00:04:31.625 --> 00:04:37.792
so that each European Council
is a productive Council.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:48.458
There is a political will to break some
taboos and to find an agreement finally.

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:51.458
If only one person doesn't agree,
there is no agreement.

00:04:52.083 --> 00:04:56.999
And so, at lots of meetings we've had,

00:04:57.125 --> 00:05:00.792
I've had to find a very special solution
for just one country.

00:05:01.166 --> 00:05:05.917
The President of the European Parliament
coordinates all the Parliament's tasks.

00:05:07.375 --> 00:05:09.625
When I chair the plenary
I oversee everything.

00:05:09.792 --> 00:05:13.667
It is not easy to keep eye contact
with so many members.

00:05:13.999 --> 00:05:17.250
Colleagues, please listen a moment.

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:21.834
I think we need to be clear
on one thing regarding this house.

00:05:21.999 --> 00:05:24.834
This house is a democratic institution!

00:05:24.999 --> 00:05:28.375
Myself I have to confess,
it is sometimes hard to hold back.

00:05:28.542 --> 00:05:32.999
I would like to take part in the
discussions because I am a politician,

00:05:33.125 --> 00:05:35.458
but the President must remain neutral.

00:05:35.625 --> 00:05:39.125
The role of the President
is, of course,

00:05:39.291 --> 00:05:43.250
to give the overall political direction
and afterwards to work for consensus.

00:05:44.417 --> 00:05:46.208
In terms of my daily work

00:05:46.375 --> 00:05:50.667
I spend a lot of time working with
the other Commissioners.

00:05:50.834 --> 00:05:53.625
I also need time to
represent the European Union,

00:05:53.792 --> 00:05:56.709
at summits, with the
President of the European Council,

00:05:56.875 --> 00:06:00.083
from the United States,
to China, to Russia, to India,

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.625
to Japan and the other summits.

00:06:07.959 --> 00:06:10.542
Which is a real structural solution
to this crisis

00:06:10.709 --> 00:06:12.208
while we receive nothing at all.

00:06:12.375 --> 00:06:15.625
This can't go on.
Montesquieu is turning in his grave.

00:06:15.792 --> 00:06:19.667
Parliament should reflect
the reality of society

00:06:19.834 --> 00:06:23.000
and in society it is also noisy.
People are noisy too.

00:06:23.166 --> 00:06:26.083
Go to a pub, go to a bistro

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:28.500
and listen to a political discussion.

00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:31.083
That is also noisy,
there are also conflicts.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:38.625
The European Council operates behind
closed doors, that's a huge difference,

00:06:38.792 --> 00:06:42.083
because we can talk to each other
face–to–face and openly.

00:06:42.875 --> 00:06:48.083
But I was surprised the first time I
took part as Belgian Prime Minister

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:51.709
that everyone was on first name terms.

00:06:51.875 --> 00:06:56.458
I suddenly had to say Nicolas,
Angela, they called me Herman.

00:06:56.625 --> 00:07:00.500
It's quite a strange experience.

00:07:00.667 --> 00:07:02.834
But I saw there really is a team spirit.

00:07:02.999 --> 00:07:07.750
You have personal contact
with each member of the Council.

00:07:07.917 --> 00:07:14.125
Knowing the background
of each one's position is important.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:18.458
I think it is very important that
you hear what other people say.

00:07:18.625 --> 00:07:20.333
That you really listen.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:22.750
Not just give them the floor
and say thank you,

00:07:22.917 --> 00:07:24.083
but you really listen.

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:27.500
Understanding the other's position

00:07:27.667 --> 00:07:33.583
is a key element in reaching decisions
on a European level.

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:39.667
What I see here is great independence
and dedication to the European cause.

00:07:39.875 --> 00:07:43.417
My experience is,
and I think this is interesting,

00:07:43.583 --> 00:07:48.250
that ideological differences
don't count in the European Commission.

00:07:48.417 --> 00:07:50.959
I can say they are almost irrelevant.

00:07:51.083 --> 00:07:54.959
Myself, I say that as President of
the Commission my party is Europe.

00:07:55.083 --> 00:07:56.875
And I really mean it.
That is my party.

00:08:02.834 --> 00:08:05.625
In the 21st century
identity and security

00:08:05.792 --> 00:08:11.166
cannot be defended
only via national structures.

00:08:11.333 --> 00:08:14.834
You need a power that goes further
than the national level.

00:08:14.999 --> 00:08:16.625
And this power must be Europe.

00:08:16.792 --> 00:08:19.999
The European Union
is not just about the market,

00:08:20.208 --> 00:08:25.458
it is a project of peace and also
a project of freedom and democracy.

00:08:25.625 --> 00:08:31.333
I think, more than ever in the 21st
century with a globalised world,

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:34.083
it is important that we stand together.

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:39.792
We are the first generation
that has not experienced war.

00:08:40.458 --> 00:08:47.333
And this is a legacy we should pass on
to our children and grandchildren

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.458
that is why we fight hard
for Europe.

00:08:49.625 --> 00:08:53.542
Not just for economic and monetary
reasons, as important as they are.

00:08:53.709 --> 00:08:57.250
We fight also
to keep this European idea intact.

